MadSMAUG — License Notice
==========================

MadSMAUG is a port of SMAUG 1.8 to the Mad-C (madc) language. Because
SMAUG 1.8 is itself derived from Merc, which is derived from DikuMUD,
the source files in this repository inherit a stack of license
obligations from each upstream layer.

Applicable licenses, preserved verbatim:

  * LICENSE.diku   — Original DikuMUD license (pre-2020).
  * LICENSE.merc   — Merc 2.x license (extends Diku).
  * LICENSE.smaug  — SMAUG 1.8 license (extends Merc).

All three apply to every source file in this repository that is
derived from SMAUG code (i.e. the contents of `src/` and
`upstream/smaug1.8.tgz`). You must read and comply with all three.

Short summary of the combined obligations (not a substitute for
reading the actual licenses):

  * Non-commercial only. You must NOT charge money for MUDs running
    this code, or for the right to play on one. See LICENSE.diku
    and LICENSE.smaug.
  * Preserve attribution. Original author credits, copyright notices,
    and the login-screen / help-file acknowledgements required by
    the Diku and SMAUG licenses must remain intact.
  * Share source. Derivative works must make source available on the
    same terms.
  * Compensation in bug reports. Per the Merc license, if you find
    a bug you are asked (not required) to report it upstream.

A note on the 2020 DikuMUD relicense
------------------------------------

In 2020, the original DikuMUD team (Hans H. Staerfeldt, Katja Nyboe,
Tom Madsen, Michael Seifert, Sebastian Hammer) re-released the
*original DikuMUD codebase* under the GNU LGPL. That relicense applies
to *their* original Diku code, but does NOT retroactively change the
licenses on derivative works (Merc, SMAUG) made before 2020 under the
older Diku terms. Merc and SMAUG remain governed by LICENSE.merc and
LICENSE.smaug respectively, and the Diku obligations from that era
still flow through into them. See LICENSE.smaug's own preamble for
the authors' intent here.

If you are unsure whether a particular use is permitted, consult the
actual license text of each layer, and err on the side of the most
restrictive.

The madc tool
-------------

The Mad-C compiler itself is a separate project with its own license
(MPL 2.0). This repository depends on madc at build time, but madc
is not covered by the licenses listed here:

  * madc repository: https://github.com/derekbsnider/madc
  * madc license: Mozilla Public License 2.0
